  "summary": "Both arms preserve most source predicates on the structured audit-style comments, and their failures cluster on short conversational sources with hedges, qualifiers, and suggestion blocks. A's characteristic failures are dropped action qualifiers and scopes (\"in this section\", \"(longer-term)\", the indented suggestion block) plus one invented severity claim, while B's are dropped certainty and quantifier markers (\"likely\", \"I personally think\", \"other adapters in this repo\", \"will make\") and two boundary errors: a suggestion-block context line promoted to a requested action and a hedged improvement relabeled as an optional follow-up. Net counts are close: A 22 fact-safe / 21 action-locked / 18 both, B 21 / 22 / 19."
